  "id": "inner-psychophysics",
  "term": "inner psychophysics",
  "definition": "In Fechner’s historical usage, inner psychophysics is the part of psychophysics concerned with the intervening process between a stimulus and apperception. It refers to mental functioning as distinct from the outward relation of stimulus to apperception.",
